NOTES
=====

1. Keep component-wise multiplication/division explicit rather than
   overloading Vec2 * Vec2 unless you have a very deliberate reason.

2. length_squared() and distance_squared() should exist alongside
   length() and distance() because avoiding sqrt is frequently useful.

3. For floating-point vectors, approximate equality should be explicit;
   do not make PartialEq pretend that floating-point equality is
   approximate.

4. Consider Point2<T> before adding lots of geometry-specific behavior
   to Vec2. A point represents a location; a vector represents a
   displacement/direction.

5. Consider a Rotation2 type before adding many rotation-specific
   methods.

6. Keep scalar functions such as sin/cos/log/etc. behind a coherent
   component-wise API if you decide to support them.

7. Consider const fn, no_std, generic scalar traits, and SIMD before
   committing too deeply to the public API. These choices can affect
   signatures throughout the crate.